{
  // Static-assets Worker: the site is two documents plus a hero image, so there is
  // no Worker script and no `main`. See docs/adr/0006-landing-page-and-app-paths.md.
  //
  // `not_found_handling` MUST NOT be "single-page-application": that value would
  // serve dist/index.html — the Landing Page — for every unmatched path, including
  // under /app/. `404-page` serves public/404.html instead.
  //
  // `html_handling` is deliberately unset: the default `auto-trailing-slash` already
  // serves /app (307 to /app/) from dist/app/index.html, redirecting the two to the
  // canonical spec form.
  //
  // /api/* is reserved for the planned backend and claimed by nothing here.
  //
  // `comp3tive` is the LIVE Worker's real name, not a placeholder. The deployed
  // origin is https://comp3tive.dimasawardhana.workers.dev/, and the name is the
  // first label of that host: a workers.dev URL is always `<worker>.<account>`.
  // Recorded 2026-10-13, verified by `curl` rather than by reading this file
  // back — see docs/ROADMAP.md, gate 3. Deploying this config updates that
  // Worker; it does not create a second one.
  //
  // A custom domain is still needed before any passkey is registered, and that
  // is a Phase E decision rather than a deploy one: a workers.dev host is on the
  // Public Suffix List's private section, so it can never share a credential with
  // a custom domain (docs/adr/0008-account-identity.md).
  // The D1 binding is declared now, ahead of the Worker script that will read it,
  // because the database exists and a binding is how a database stops being an
  // unrecorded remote resource. `main` and `assets.run_worker_first` are NOT here
  // yet, and that is deliberate: `main` would name `server/index.ts` before it
  // exists, and a config that points at a missing file breaks `wrangler deploy`
  // for a site that is otherwise live. Both arrive with the script (TASK-114).
  // Wrangler accepts a `d1_databases` block with no `main` and exposes it as
  // `env.DB`, verified by `deploy --dry-run` on 2026-10-15.
  //
  // `comp3tive-db` is the database's real name and `database_id` is its real id,
  // created 2026-10-15. A database id is an identifier, not a secret: what stays
  // out of the repo is the Worker's runtime secrets. The binding is `DB` — not
  // wrangler's suggested `comp3tive_db` — since one database needs no
  // disambiguating prefix, and `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-28-account-and-durability.md`
  // freezes that name for `server/storage.ts` to consume.
  //
  // Local development needs no account and no real id: `wrangler d1 execute
  // --local` runs against a placeholder `database_id`, so `npm run dev` and the
  // unit tests never touch Cloudflare.
  "name": "comp3tive",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-14",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist",
    "not_found_handling": "404-page"
  },
  "d1_databases": [
    {
      "binding": "DB",
      "database_name": "comp3tive-db",
      "database_id": "d73ee1c8-7089-4da6-8ca4-91f5626b1a3a"
    }
  ]
}
